        "PMC8398136::rubric_gaps::007::03aa0ecbf3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The elevated lattice friction impedes screw-dislocation motion and necessitates kink-pair nucleation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::rubric_gaps::007::fbab79c0fa"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yield onset in single-crystal FeNiCrMn is controlled by thermally activated kink-pair nucleation on screw dislocations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::rubric_gaps::007::fbab79c0fa"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chemical disorder creates a fluctuating potential-energy landscape with high Peierls stress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8357793::rubric_gaps::007::fbab79c0fa",
        "PMC8398136::rubric_gaps::007::03aa0ecbf3"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kink-pair nucleation, rather than dislocation glide velocity, is the rate-limiting event during yielding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dominance of the thermally activated nucleation barrier decouples yield strength from strain rate.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yield strength decreases strongly as temperature increases from cryogenic temperatures toward 600 K.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Yield strength has negligible dependence on strain rate over approximately 10^-4 to 10^2 s^-1.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The FCC structure is retained without an FCC-to-BCC transformation during yielding.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
